accessibility-gate = every future correction proposal explanation approval rejection execution recovery undo or audit surface must expose the same native semantics nonvisually and remain fully operable without sight or pointer dependence
claim = success will establish accessible human approval and rejection of a structurally derived correction proposal without executing that proposal
claim = success will encode rejection as the native identity action rather than a host-language boolean cancel flag
claim = success will establish equivalent visual UIA speech and braille presentation of the proposal and the human decision
claim = success will not authorize or execute correction and will not establish autonomous recovery
